From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0248: QSEE client, Goodix fingerprint probe (milestone 1)

Boot-arg qsee=1 enables sysctl kern.sweet_qsee (1 run, 2 sensor GPIOs off,
3 APP_SHUTDOWN goodixfp). Op 1: QSEE version and whitelist feature, APP_LOOKUP
keymaster64 and goodixfp, the sensor powered (RPM ldoa9 1.8 V, gpio65 high,
gpio104 reset pulse), APP_START goodixfp (mdt + b00..b07 from modem_a, at
0xE8000000: 16 MB of the unmanaged low-bank hole), then SENSOR PRE_DETECT and
DETECT_SENSOR through libgf_hal's envelope with SEND_DATA(_WHITELIST).
Listener requests are logged and answered FAILURE; nothing is written to any
partition. TopazModem exports its modem-partition file reader and an RPM LDO
vote. Without qsee=1 nothing new runs.
---
